 course  something has to go wrong there's a shot  of jimmy and kim where i believe they're  listening in on the call because you see  the box for one of his burner phones on  the table he's making a reeling him in  motion with his hands like he's holding  a fishing pole and you can see that this  is making kim smile so at least for a  while they think everything's working  out probably what seems like the most  critical scene in the teaser is also  quick and inconclusive you hear howard  say i'm going to figure out what the  hell's happening you see him turn his  head and i'd like to say the effects of  the drug have kicked in but you can't  really tell he looks at a painting of  chuck and it looks like he has a  revelation is this just him feeling  whacked out or is it him realizing he's  about to fall into a trap after that you  see him running up the stairs and cliff  coming after him calling his name from  the landing i hope i'm not wrong in  thinking he's running towards his office  since i couldn't find any evidence that  it was actually on the top floor and  it's really hard to craft a scenario on  two seconds of footage but if i had to  guess he's just made the accusation and  is now going to get the evidence the  photos which won't be there anymore if  this really is that good of a scam that  would sort of be the ideal outcome for  kim and jimmy alternately he could just  be freaking out from the drug's effects  since they established that he drinks a  non-caffeinated tea perhaps he looked  like a kook he started talking to  chuck's painting and then ran out of the  room because he didn't know what was  happening this would still validate  cliff's concerns which is the goal of  the plan so the outcome would be similar  the problem with either of these is that  jimmy and kim win so there would almost  have to be a fall that follows that i  don't imagine i'm alone in thinking that  whatever goes wrong here will be the  first step in the sequence of events  that explain why kim isn't around and  breaking bad some unintended consequence  has to come out of this meticulously  planned scheme howard could figure out  what they're doing and outmaneuver them  stop the plan from working but there  doesn't feel like there's a conclusion  built into that nothing that we've seen  so far about this back and forth with  howard leads us to believe that it's  gonna be the entire season there's a lot  of other stuff that needs to happen  howard could have an adverse reaction i  don't really think he'll die i'm not  expecting that for the character but he  could or he could have a stroke or  something along those lines maybe he has  a fall he's running around like a  lunatic maybe he falls down throughout  this season the show has been making a  point of trying to make these teasers  tricky making us think something will  happen when it doesn't and i think that  on top of everything else really makes  it impossible to guess but that also  makes it all the more fun i guess the  biggest takeaway i had from this is  we're going to get that payoff for the  last three episodes which were mostly  set up  there's also some gus mike and lalo in  the trailer god seems to be doing some  of the charity work we know he does from  breaking bad it looks like mike takes  him aside and plays him something on a  tape recorder this is a little out of  place but contextually it almost has to  be connected to him finding out what  lalo's up to mike tells him that they  need home court advantage and that seems  to line up with them setting a trap for  lalo where they can control things with  their security team there's a shot of  lalo walking down a hallway with a sign  on the wall which is something i guess  you might see in a truck stop in the u.s  it's for a shower that you can rent for  ten dollars an hour the most interesting  thing is that it's not in spanish or  german and seems to confirm that he's  back in the states which gets me really  excited 