hat explain why kim isn't around and  breaking bad some unintended consequence  has to come out of this meticulously  planned scheme howard could figure out  what they're doing and outmaneuver them  stop the plan from working but there  doesn't feel like there's a conclusion  built into that nothing that we've seen  so far about this back and forth with  howard leads us to believe that it's  gonna be the entire season there's a lot  of other stuff that needs to happen  howard could have an adverse reaction i  don't really think he'll die i'm not  expecting that for the character but he  could or he could have a stroke or  something along those lines maybe he has  a fall he's running around like a  lunatic maybe he falls down throughout  this season the show has been making a  point of trying to make these teasers  tricky making us think something will  happen when it doesn't and i think that  on top of everything else really makes  it impossible to guess but that also  makes it all the more fun i guess the  biggest takeaway i had from this is  we're going to get that payoff for the  last three episodes which were mostly  set up  there's also some gus mike and lalo in  the trailer god seems to be doing some  of the charity work we know he does from  breaking bad it looks like mike takes  him aside and plays him something on a  tape recorder this is a little out of  place but contextually it almost has to  be connected to him finding out what  lalo's up to mike tells him that they  need home court advantage and that seems  to line up with them setting a trap for  lalo where they can control things with  their security team there's a shot of  lalo walking down a hallway with a sign  on the wall which is something i guess  you might see in a truck stop in the u.s  it's for a shower that you can rent for  ten dollars an hour the most interesting  thing is that it's not in spanish or  german and seems to confirm that he's  back in the states which gets me really  excited there's another shot of him  setting a timer and going to sleep in a  car which could be related to this trip  but it almost looks like it still has  that blue german tint they used and i  can't think of a good reason we would  need to see any more of his time there  so i'm hoping this is all in the u.s too  there's only one completely random shot  of binoculars that look like the same  ones kim used in episode 1. there's also  a promo photo of hector on the phone  which you would guess might be lalo  telling him about his plan to get proof  but who knows someone's going to call  hector on the phone and that's pretty  much it peter gould did say this episode  would end with a pretty major  cliffhanger so we have that to think  about during the break i think it's  worth mentioning again that they didn't  write the season in two parts i'm  expecting this to be a better place to  break than at the end of episode six  which if you think about it would have  been pretty bad but i'm trying not to  have too crazy of an expectation that  everything is going to get wrapped up or  something like that going into the  second half which is going to be  completely different and i do think  there's a high likelihood that we'll see  the walt and jesse appearance in this  episode not because of anything that was  on imdb or any of that but it just seems  like the perfect time to introduce them  because you would get a lot of buzz out  of it and maybe some people that haven't  been watching will decide to catch up  before the second half of the season  starts if you're going to introduce them  say in a teaser something like a flash  forward before the break seems a lot  better than after thomas schnauz did  write and direct this episode which is a  good sign his last episode was 509 with  that famous kim and lalo showdown and he  usually does important ones and i think  that's a good place to leave things  let me know what you think will happen  in the comments and how you think things  will go wrong for kim and jimmy please  like this video if you enjoyed it please  subscribe to my channel if you haven't  already and thanks for watching i'll  talk to you soon


